.2020.9242570"},{"key":"ref11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-031-72215-8_15"},{"key":"ref12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/ISPA54004.2022.9786284"},{"key":"ref13","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.dajour.2022.100073"},{"key":"ref14","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s42452-019-1926-x"},{"key":"ref15","article-title":"Imdb movie reviews","author":"Dapat","year":"2023","journal-title":"Kaggle"}],"event":{"name":"2025 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Data Engineering (AIDE)","start":{"date-parts":[[2025,2,6]]},"location":"Nitte, India","end":{"date-parts":[[2025,2,7]]}},"container-title":["2025 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Data Engineering (AIDE)"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/10985945\/10986773\/10987367.pdf?arnumber=10987367","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,13]],"date-time":"2025-05-13T06:29:00Z","timestamp":1747117740000},"score":41.53174,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/10987367\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,2,6]]},"references-count":15,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/aide64228.2025.10987367","published":{"date-parts":[[2025,2,6]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,16]],"date-time":"2025-11-16T13:54:18Z","timestamp":1763301258637,"version":"3.45.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"International Journal for Multidisciplinary Research (IJFMR)","issue":"6","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["IJFMR"],"abstract":"<jats:p>This study presents a sentiment analysis system for IMDb movie reviews using Multinomial and Bernoulli Naive Bayes classifiers with Laplace smoothing. After preprocessing text data, both models were evaluated using 5-fold cross-validation. Results show that Multinomial Naive Bayes outperforms Bernoulli Naive Bayes, achieving higher accuracy and better handling of word frequency information in long textual reviews.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.36948\/ijfmr.2025.v07i06.60198","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,16]],"date-time":"2025-11-16T13:49:11Z","timestamp":1763300951000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["IMDb Sentiment Analysis Using Naive Bayes :Multinomial and Bernoulli Models with LaplaceSmoothing and 5-Fold Cross Validation"],"prefix":"10.36948","volume":"7","author":[{"given":"Lija","family":"Mishra","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"23064","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,13]]},"container-title":["International Journal For Multidisciplinary Research"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ijfmr.com\/papers\/2025\/6\/60198.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,16]],"date-time":"2025-11-16T13:49:16Z","timestamp":1763300956000},"score":41.37658,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ijfmr.com\/research-paper.php?id=60198"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,13]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"6","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.36948\/ijfmr.2025.v07i06.60198","ISSN":["2582-2160"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2582-2160","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,13]]},"article-number":"60198"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,10]],"date-time":"2025-07-10T10:40:10Z","timestamp":1752144010544,"version":"3.41.2"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Nepal Journals Online (JOL)","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,30]],"date-time":"2025-05-30T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1748563200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["J. Eng. Sci."],"abstract":"<jats:p>Sentiment analysis is a powerful tool for understanding public opinion, especially in the entertainment industry. Opinion in the form of text reviews plays a significant role in the success of a movie. Text-based data analysis is extensively used to recognize opinion sentiments. Achieving the proper sentiment for classification is crucial for both consumers and organizations. Handling large and complex data can pose more challenges during classification. This quantitative research is focused on classifying the sentiments of the IMDb movie review dataset using supervised Machine Learning (ML) models such as Naive Bayes (NB) and Support Vector Machines (SVM). The sentiments were classified as positive and negative to identify best-fit models for the large-scale review classification. 50,000 IMDb movie reviews went through preprocessing and feature extraction to transform unprocessed text input into numerical form, deploying Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF). Eventually, the split between positive and negative ratings was even distributed. SVM and NB models were trained and assessed on various train-test splits to ensure robust model evaluation. Precision, Recall, and F1 Score were performance metrics applied to calculate the efficiency of models. Based on the report, the SVM model outperformed Naive Bayes regarding accuracy. SVM achieved an average accuracy of 88%, while Naive Bayes achieved 85%. This research can significantly aid filmmakers in understanding viewer preferences, which is crucial for market strategy and content creation.\nKeywords: IMDb Movie Review; Naive Bayes; SVM; TF-IDF<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3126\/jes2.v4i1.70138","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,30]],"date-time":"2025-05-30T08:41:22Z","timestamp":1748594482000},"page":"56-68","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Sentiment Analysis of IMDb Movie Reviews Using SVM and Naive Bayes Classifier"],"prefix":"10.3126","volume":"4","author":[{"given":"Dhurba","family":"Subedi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"family":"Nabin Lamichhane","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Nabaraj","family":"Subedi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"1670","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,30]]},"container-title":["Journal of Engineering and Sciences"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.nepjol.info\/index.php\/jes2\/article\/download\/70138\/60783","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/www.nepjol.info\/index.php\/jes2\/article\/download\/70138\/60783","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,10]],"date-time":"2025-07-10T10:08:29Z","timestamp":1752142109000},"score":40.554985,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.nepjol.info\/index.php\/jes2\/article\/view\/70138"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,30]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,30]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3126\/jes2.v4i1.70138","ISSN":["2976-1190"],"issn-type":[{"type":"electronic","value":"2976-1190"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,30]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,3]],"date-time":"2026-02-03T17:05:40Z","timestamp":1770138340605,"version":"3.49.0"},"reference-count":15,"publisher":"IEEE","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]],"date-time":"2021-07-29T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1627516800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/Xplorehelp\/downloads\/license-information\/IEEE.html"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]],"date-time":"2021-07-29T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1627516800000},"content-version":"stm-asf","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.15223\/policy-029"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]],"date-time":"2021-07-29T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1627516800000},"content-version":"stm-asf","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.15223\/policy-037"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]]},"DOI":"10.1109\/icera53111.2021.9538763","type":"proceedings-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,9,20]],"date-time":"2021-09-20T21:34:09Z","timestamp":1632173649000},"page":"99-103","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":8,"title":["Implementation of Sentiment Analysis Movie Review based on IMDB with Naive Bayes Using Information Gain on Feature Selection"],"prefix":"10.1109","author":[{"given":"Meta","family":"Mahyarani","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Adiwijaya","family":"Adiwijaya","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Said Al","family":"Faraby","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Mahendra","family":"Dwifebri","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"263","reference":[{"key":"ref10","article-title":"Fast and Accurate Sentiment Classification Using an Enhanced Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Model","author":"narayanan","year":"2013","journal-title":"Internation Coference on Intelligent Data Engineering and Automated Learning"},{"key":"ref11","author":"yenter","year":"2017","journal-title":"Deep CNN-LSTM with Combined Kernels from Multiple Branches for IMDb Review Sentiment Analysis"},{"key":"ref12","author":"tarimer","year":"2019","journal-title":"Sentiment Analysis on IMDB Movie Comments and Twitter Data by Machine Learning and Vector Space Techniques"},{"key":"ref13","author":"purnomoputra","year":"2019","journal-title":"Sentiment Analysis of Movie Reviews using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Method with Gini Index Feature Selection"},{"key":"ref14","author":"tripathi","year":"2020","journal-title":"Analyzing Sentiment using IMDb Dataset"},{"key":"ref15","author":"rahul shah","year":"2021","journal-title":"Movie Stats Sentiment Analysis of IMDB Reviews and Tweets of a Movie Using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Classifier"},{"key":"ref4","article-title":"Sentiment Analysis of Review Datasets using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes and K-NN Classifier","author":"dey","year":"2016","journal-title":"arXiv Cornell University Computer Science Information Retrieval"},{"key":"ref3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/ACCESS.2019.2909919"},{"key":"ref6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.22364\/bjmc.2017.5.4.06"},{"key":"ref5","article-title":"On the Feature Selection and Classification Based on Information Gain for Document Sentiment Analysis","author":"indah pratiwi","year":"2018","journal-title":"Applied Computational Intelligence and Soft Computing 2018"},{"key":"ref8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5120\/ijca2017916005"},{"key":"ref7","article-title":"Sentiment Analysis on Twitter Posts : An analysis of Positive or Negative Opinion on Gojek","author":"pertiwi","year":"2017","journal-title":"Proc of 2017 4th Int Conf on Information Tech Computer and Electrical Engineering (ICITACEE)"},{"key":"ref2","article-title":"Sentiment Analysis on IMDb Movie Reviews Using Hybrid Feature Extraction Method","author":"keerthi kumar","year":"2018","journal-title":"International Journal of Interactive Multimedia and Artificial Intelligence"},{"key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-319-96136-1_15"},{"key":"ref9","first-page":"54","article-title":"Sentimental Analysis of Tweets Using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Algorithm","volume":"35","author":"vadivukarassi","year":"2017","journal-title":"World Applied Sciences Journal"}],"event":{"name":"2021 3rd International Conference on Electronics Representation and Algorithm (ICERA)","location":"Yogyakarta, Indonesia","start":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]]},"end":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,30]]}},"container-title":["2021 3rd International Conference on Electronics Representation and Algorithm (ICERA)"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx7\/9538521\/9538631\/09538763.pdf?arnumber=9538763","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,10]],"date-time":"2022-05-10T15:46:10Z","timestamp":1652197570000},"score":37.497093,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/9538763\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]]},"references-count":15,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icera53111.2021.9538763","published":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,31]],"date-time":"2025-12-31T02:49:04Z","timestamp":1767149344647,"version":"3.48.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Politeknik Negeri Batam","issue":"6","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]],"date-time":"2025-12-06T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1764979200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-sa\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["JAIC"],"abstract":"<jats:p>This study aims to classify user opinions on IMDb movie reviews using the Multinomial Na\u00efve Bayes algorithm. The dataset consists of 50,000 reviews, evenly distributed between 25,000 positive and 25,000 negative reviews. The preprocessing stage includes cleaning, case folding, stopword removal, tokenization, and lemmatization using the NLTK library. Text features are represented through the TF-IDF method to capture the significance of each word in the documents. The Multinomial Na\u00efve Bayes model was trained using the hold-out validation technique with an 80:20 split for training and testing data. Hyperparameter tuning of \u03b1 (Laplace smoothing) was conducted to enhance model stability and accuracy. The model\u2019s performance was evaluated using accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score metrics, supported by a confusion matrix visualization. The results show that the model achieved an accuracy of 87%, with precision of 87.9%, recall of 85.4%, and an F1-score of 86.6%. In comparison, Logistic Regression as a baseline algorithm achieved an accuracy of 91%. Nevertheless, the Na\u00efve Bayes algorithm remains competitive and computationally efficient for large-scale text data, making it highly relevant for sentiment analysis of movie reviews.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.30871\/jaic.v9i6.9831","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,31]],"date-time":"2025-12-31T02:36:41Z","timestamp":1767148601000},"page":"3168-3176","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Opinion Classification on IMDb Reviews Using Na\u00efve Bayes Algorithm"],"prefix":"10.30871","volume":"9","author":[{"given":"Amiliya","family":"Putri","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Khothibul","family":"Umam","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hery","family":"Mustofa","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"12321","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]]},"container-title":["Journal of Applied Informatics and Computing"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.polibatam.ac.id\/index.php\/JAIC\/article\/download\/9831\/3178","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.polibatam.ac.id\/index.php\/JAIC\/article\/download\/9831\/3178","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,31]],"date-time":"2025-12-31T02:39:09Z","timestamp":1767148749000},"score":37.488773,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.polibatam.ac.id\/index.php\/JAIC\/article\/view\/9831"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"6","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,12]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.30871\/jaic.v9i6.9831","ISSN":["2548-6861"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2548-6861","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T09:38:05Z","timestamp":1772271485699,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"PeerJ","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.3272\/supp-3","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,30]],"date-time":"2025-10-30T08:31:51Z","timestamp":1761813111000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Supplemental Information 3: Implementing Naive Bayes Classification."],"prefix":"10.7717","member":"4443","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,30]],"date-time":"2025-10-30T08:31:54Z","timestamp":1761813114000},"score":34.675293,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/peerj.com\/articles\/cs-3272\/supp-3"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7717\/peerj-cs.3272\/supp-3","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.3272","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"institution":[{"name":"Research Square"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,20]],"date-time":"2024-09-20T16:54:09Z","timestamp":1726851249558},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,9]]},"group-title":"In Review","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Research Square Platform LLC","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,9]],"date-time":"2022-05-09T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1652054400000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"accepted":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,6]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n        <jats:p>Sentiment analysis has emerged as a powerful method to extract polarization of opinion from text. A vast number of prominent sentiment analysis methods can be categorized into rule-based method, lexicon-based method, machine learning method, and deep learning, and ontology-based method. An increasing interest toward sentiment analysis is motivated, among others, by some successful use cases of sentiment analysis in several domains and availability of enormous data as the result of big data explosion in the past ten years. The objective of this study is to identify some latest study reports that represent various trends of sentiment analysis. We implemented sentiment analysis for Arabic tweets, we applied SVM and Naive Bayes algorithms.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.21203\/rs.3.rs-1631367\/v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,9]],"date-time":"2022-05-09T15:29:48Z","timestamp":1652110188000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["SVM and Naive Bayes for Sentiment Analysis in Arabic"],"prefix":"10.21203","author":[{"given":"Ahmed","family":"Mohamed","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Cairo University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"8761","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.researchsquare.com\/article\/rs-1631367\/v1","content-type":"text\/html","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/www.researchsquare.com\/article\/rs-1631367\/v1.html","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,9]],"date-time":"2022-05-09T15:29:55Z","timestamp":1652110195000},"score":34.178284,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.researchsquare.com\/article\/rs-1631367\/v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,9]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.21203\/rs.3.rs-1631367\/v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,9]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,25]],"date-time":"2023-04-25T04:38:55Z","timestamp":1682397535923},"d