ole":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Mohd Zaliman Mohd","family":"Yusoff","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Information Technology, Universiti Tenaga Nasional, Putrajaya, Malaysia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"263","reference":[{"key":"ref4","article-title":"Data Mining for Tweet Sentiment Classification","author":"groot","year":"2012","journal-title":"Utrecht University Utrecht Netherlands"},{"key":"ref3","article-title":"Citius: A Naive-Bayes Strategy for Sentiment Analysis on English Tweets","author":"pablo","year":"2014","journal-title":"Proceedings of the 8th International Workshop on Semantic Evaluation (SemEval 2014)"},{"key":"ref6","article-title":"A Machine Learning Approach to Twitter User Classification","author":"marco","year":"2011","journal-title":"Proceedings of the Fifth International AAAI Conference on Weblogs and Social Media"},{"key":"ref5","first-page":"959","article-title":"Important Features Selection During Sentiment","volume":"26","author":"muhammad","year":"2014","journal-title":"Sci int(Lahore)"},{"key":"ref8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/asi.4630270302"},{"key":"ref7","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1145\/321921.321930"},{"key":"ref2","article-title":"Analysis and Classification","author":"horn","year":"2010","journal-title":"IAIK Graz University of Technology Graz Austria"},{"journal-title":"Introduction to Information Retrieval","year":"2008","author":"christopher","key":"ref1"}],"event":{"name":"2015 IEEE Conference on e-Learning, e-Management and e-Services (IC3e)","start":{"date-parts":[[2015,8,24]]},"location":"Melaka, Malaysia","end":{"date-parts":[[2015,8,26]]}},"container-title":["2015 IEEE Conference on e-Learning, e-Management and e-Services (IC3e)"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx7\/7395550\/7403412\/07403510.pdf?arnumber=7403510","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,8,23]],"date-time":"2025-08-23T00:28:57Z","timestamp":1755908937000},"score":32.56302,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/7403510\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2015,8]]},"references-count":8,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/ic3e.2015.7403510","published":{"date-parts":[[2015,8]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,12]],"date-time":"2026-03-12T20:51:32Z","timestamp":1773348692384,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Pusat Penelitian dan Pengabdian Pada Masyarakat Universitas Respati Yogyakarta","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,30]],"date-time":"2025-06-30T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1751241600000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-sa\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ijicom"],"abstract":"<jats:p>The rapid advancement of technology has encouraged the use of Artificial Intelligence in various sectors, including higher education. Among students, Artificial Intelligence was used to support learning activities, although it posed ethical concerns such as technological dependency and the risk of plagiarism. This study aimed to examine students\u2019 sentiment toward the use of Artificial Intelligence in academic contexts. Data were collected through an online survey with a total of 498 responses, consisting of 347 positive sentiments and 151 negative sentiments. The classification process employed the Multinomial Na\u00efve Bayes (MNB) algorithm using training data proportions of 60%, 70%, 80%, and 90%, along with combinations of unigram, bigram, and trigram features. The highest accuracy of 0.84 was obtained using 90% training data with the combination of all three features. As a comparison, the Random Forest algorithm achieved its highest accuracy of 0.86 using unigram features with the same training proportion. The results showed that both algorithms performed well in sentiment classification, with Random Forest slightly outperforming. Furthermore, the findings revealed variations in students\u2019 adherence to academic ethics regarding the use of Artificial Intelligence.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.35842\/ijicom.v7i1.122","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,3]],"date-time":"2025-12-03T05:20:25Z","timestamp":1764739225000},"page":"279-290","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Sentiment Classification of Student Opinions on AI Utilization Using Naive Bayes Algorithm"],"prefix":"10.35842","volume":"7","author":[{"given":"Rista","family":"Melinda Yuniar","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Sri","family":"Mulyati","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"21514","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,30]]},"container-title":["International Journal of Informatics and Computation"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/ijicom.respati.ac.id\/index.php\/ijicom\/article\/download\/122\/93","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/ijicom.respati.ac.id\/index.php\/ijicom\/article\/download\/122\/93","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,3]],"date-time":"2025-12-03T05:20:26Z","timestamp":1764739226000},"score":32.499588,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ijicom.respati.ac.id\/index.php\/ijicom\/article\/view\/122"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,30]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,30]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.35842\/ijicom.v7i1.122","ISSN":["2714-5263","2685-8711"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2714-5263","type":"electronic"},{"value":"2685-8711","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,30]]}